WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:08.153
Begin by framing Introduction to Co-op and
Course Purpose as a question about inputs,

2
00:00:08.153 --> 00:00:10.468
decisions, and observable results.

3
00:00:10.468 --> 00:00:16.311
This seminar helps students prepare for
Computer Science co-operative education

4
00:00:16.311 --> 00:00:22.737
employment ("co-op") by developing job search
strategies and materials, and reviewing

5
00:00:22.737 --> 00:00:23.906
relevant policies.

6
00:00:23.906 --> 00:00:29.985
Consider this worked case: A second-year
COMPSCI-BS student must complete this course

7
00:00:29.985 --> 00:00:33.531
before applying for a summer co-op position.

8
00:00:33.531 --> 00:00:40.633
List the givens before choosing a method,
because an unstated assumption can change the

9
00:00:40.633 --> 00:00:41.140
conclusion.

10
00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.796
This establishes the vocabulary and scope
needed for the remaining sections.

11
00:00:46.922 --> 00:00:53.856
Now define Prerequisites and Eligibility
precisely enough that another learner could

12
00:00:53.856 --> 00:00:55.747
